0.27.426.855 D Parsed message: {"role":"assistant","content":"\nI'll help you implement this Kanban board application. Let's start with the project initialization and file structure setup.\n","reasoning_content":"Let's start by breaking down the task and figuring out what files we need to create. This is a collaborative Kanban board application with a Node.js backend using PGLite for embedded PostgreSQL and a Vanilla JS/Vite frontend.\n\nFirst, let's handle the project initialization as per section 1:\n\n1.1 Initialize the Node.js project and install backend dependencies (express, @electric-sql/pglite, cors)\n1.2 Initialize the Vanilla JS / Vite project for the frontend and install frontend dependencies\n1.3 Set up basic npm scripts for concurrently running backend and frontend development servers\n1.4 Make the app start from a fresh checkout with no manual steps\n\nFor this, we'll need:\n- A root package.json file with scripts to run both backend and frontend\n- A backend directory (e.g., \"server\") with its own package.json\n- A frontend directory (e.g., \"client\") with its own package.json (generated by Vite)\n\nThen, let's handle the backend infrastructure and database as per section 2:\n\n2.1 Set up a basic Express server with CORS and JSON body parsing\n2.2 Initialize embedded PGLite configured to write to the local file system\n2.3 Create the database initialization script with columns and cards tables\n2.4 Create the board state endpoint\n\nFor this, we'll need:\n- Server entry point (e.g., server/index.js)\n- Database initialization script (e.g., server/db/init.js)\n- API routes for board state (e.g., server/routes/board.js)\n\nNext, let's handle board mutations and real-time sync as per section 3:\n\n3.1 Implement POST /api/cards to create a card\n3.2 Implement PATCH /api/cards/:id/move to move a card\n3.3 Implement SSE endpoint GET /api/stream\n3.4 Guarantee atomic moves and broadcast only committed state\n3.5 Handle position collisions/exhaustion\n\nFor this, we'll need:\n- API routes for cards (e.g., server/routes/cards.js)\n- SSE implementation (e.g., server/sse.js)\n- Transaction handling for moves\n\nFinally, let's handle the frontend implementation as per section 4:\n\n4.1 Render columns and cards from GET /api/board\n4.2 Implement drag-and-drop\n4.3 Optimistic updates on drop\n4.4 Connect to SSE and update DOM with canonical state\n4.5 Reconcile optimistic state\n4.6 Card creation UI\n\nFor this, we'll need:\n- Frontend entry point (e.g., client/main.js)\n- HTML template (e.g., client/index.html)\n- CSS for styling (e.g., client/style.css)\n- Drag-and-drop implementation\n- SSE client implementation\n\nLet's start implementing these files one by one.","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write_file","arguments":"{\"path\":\"package.json\",\"content\":\"{\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"kanban-board\\\",\\n  \\\"version\\\": \\\"1.0.0\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Multi-user Kanban board with real-time collaboration using PGLite and SSE\\\",\\n  \\\"scripts\\\": {\\n    \\\"dev\\\": \\\"concurrently \\\\\\\"cd server && npm run dev\\\\\\\" \\\\\\\"cd client && npm run dev\\\\\\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"install\\\": \\\"cd server && npm install && cd client && npm install\\\",\\n    \\\"start\\\": \\\"cd server && npm start\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"devDependencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"concurrently\\\": \\\"^8.2.0\\\"\\n  }\\n}\"}"}}]}
